<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Medici</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1434">1434</a>–<a href="/years/1737">1737</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Medici family</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Medici was a Florentine banking family that dominated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> from 1434, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cosimo-de-medici">Cosimo the Elder</a> returned from exile. Its members included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorenzo-de-medici">Lorenzo the Magnificent</a> and the popes Leo X and Clement VII, and from 1532 they ruled as dukes of Florence and from 1569 as grand dukes of Tuscany. The main line died out in 1737, and the family's art collections remained in Florence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-medici.jpg" alt="House of Medici" width="320" height="373" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heralder · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Augmented_Arms_of_Medici.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
